00:53:50.952 --> 00:53:55.952
And it is now my pleasure to
introduce you to Sharon Kugler,

00:53:57.964 --> 00:54:00.214
Yale's University Chaplain.

00:54:01.120 --> 00:54:05.176
Chaplain Kugler joined the
Yale community in 2007,

00:54:05.176 --> 00:54:07.891
bringing with her over
two decades of experience

00:54:07.891 --> 00:54:10.270
in ministry, in higher education,

00:54:10.270 --> 00:54:15.177
interfaith collaboration, and
pastoral and social ministry.

00:54:15.177 --> 00:54:17.394
Over the past 14 years,

00:54:17.394 --> 00:54:21.237
she has cultivated a chaplaincy
that serves the needs

00:54:21.237 --> 00:54:25.756
of the richly, diverse religious
and spiritual traditions

00:54:25.756 --> 00:54:28.756
of our faculty, students, and staff.

00:54:30.408 --> 00:54:35.241
For our campus community, she
facilitates deeper dialogue,

00:54:36.580 --> 00:54:40.211
increased access, personal growth,

00:54:40.211 --> 00:54:43.119
creative educational opportunities,

00:54:43.119 --> 00:54:45.933
and pastoral leadership.

00:54:45.933 --> 00:54:48.224
Chaplain Kugler is also a lecturer

00:54:48.224 --> 00:54:51.251
of interreligious
engagement and chaplaincy

00:54:51.251 --> 00:54:53.869
at the Yale Divinity School.

00:54:53.869 --> 00:54:56.851
And so I will turn things
over to Chaplain Kugler

00:54:56.851 --> 00:54:58.518
for the benediction.

00:55:11.070 --> 00:55:14.070
- In his work, "Today is a New Day,"

00:55:14.928 --> 00:55:19.928
a piece that is both poem and
invitation to young scholars,

00:55:20.362 --> 00:55:24.945
the 2015 U.S. Poet Laureate,
Juan Felipe Herrera wrote,

00:55:26.448 --> 00:55:28.878
"Today is a new day.

00:55:28.878 --> 00:55:30.628
You are that new day!

00:55:32.450 --> 00:55:35.147
Today you are that new time.

00:55:35.147 --> 00:55:37.314
Now visible, now prepared,

00:55:38.408 --> 00:55:41.325
now filled with eagerness and hope.

00:55:42.234 --> 00:55:43.734
You are that hope.

00:55:44.601 --> 00:55:47.684
The wild born vista of new horizons."

00:55:50.386 --> 00:55:53.469
Students, faculty, staff, loved ones.

00:55:54.605 --> 00:55:59.022
You are, each and everyone,
part of a whole new Yale,

00:55:59.943 --> 00:56:03.026
a new circle of scholars and friends.

00:56:04.146 --> 00:56:08.475
What Yale was yesterday
is not what it is today

00:56:08.475 --> 00:56:11.392
or will be tomorrow because of you.

00:56:12.241 --> 00:56:15.801
Your questions will emerge and then bloom.

00:56:15.801 --> 00:56:19.051
And your fresh intellect will carry us all

00:56:19.051 --> 00:56:21.801
to a new discovery, to a new day.

00:56:23.514 --> 00:56:26.127
As we prepare to take our next steps

00:56:26.127 --> 00:56:27.735
into these new discoveries,

00:56:27.735 --> 00:56:29.568
we note our anxieties,

00:56:30.918 --> 00:56:34.723
but we also lift up our
considerable abilities

00:56:34.723 --> 00:56:38.329
and the remarkable fellowship
we will come to share

00:56:38.329 --> 00:56:39.412
in community.

00:56:40.650 --> 00:56:44.650
Let curiosity nourish us
and compassion guide us

00:56:45.595 --> 00:56:48.012
as this new creation unfolds.

00:56:49.235 --> 00:56:52.424
On this day and every day forward,

00:56:52.424 --> 00:56:56.007
may all that is holy shine upon us

00:56:56.007 --> 00:56:59.007
and tenderly bless our every breath.

00:57:00.788 --> 00:57:02.455
May we go in shalom,

00:57:03.478 --> 00:57:05.145
in salam, in shanti,

00:57:07.268 --> 00:57:08.851
may we go in peace?

00:57:09.901 --> 00:57:11.568
This is our new day.

00:57:12.634 --> 00:57:13.801
Let us begin.

